1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,111
Will a heat pump actually save you money?

2
00:00:02,231 --> 00:00:04,073
You can find out in thirty seconds.

3
00:00:04,193 --> 00:00:09,153
Grab two numbers from your bills: what you pay per kilowatt-hour of electricity,

4
00:00:09,273 --> 00:00:11,070
and what you pay per therm of gas.

5
00:00:11,190 --> 00:00:16,659
Divide the electricity price by the gas price, then multiply by twenty-seven point eight.

6
00:00:16,779 --> 00:00:23,146
That's your break-even: how efficient a heat pump has to be to beat a new ninety-five percent gas furnace.

7
00:00:23,266 --> 00:00:28,376
For example, eighteen cents and a dollar fifty a therm gives about three point three.

8
00:00:28,496 --> 00:00:31,818
A heat pump at the federal minimum is about two point two.

9
00:00:31,938 --> 00:00:34,473
So around two or lower, the heat pump should win.

10
00:00:34,593 --> 00:00:36,780
Above three, gas will most likely win.

11
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,294
Try it with your own bills.

12
00:00:38,414 --> 00:00:42,375
In thirty seconds, you'll know if a heat pump will actually save you money.
